## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with SwiftUI basics, timer handling, accessibility, and simple persistence in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI TimerPublisher and state management
- MVVM pattern with @ObservableObject and @Published
- UserDefaults for minimal persistence
- Accessibility: VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, color contrast
- Debouncing user input to prevent thrashing

## Code Example
```swift
class FocusTimerViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var remaining: Int = 0
  @Published var isRunning: Bool = false
  private var cancellable: AnyCancellable?
  func start(duration: Int) {
    remaining = duration * 60
    isRunning = true
    cancellable = Timer.publish(every: 1, on: .main, in: .common)
      .autoconnect()
      .sink { [weak self] _ in
        guard let self = self else { return }
        if self.remaining > 0 { self.remaining -= 1 } else { self.isRunning = false }
      }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle timer accuracy when the app is backgrounded?
- How would you scale to more than 3 presets and persist per-preset state?

